CHAPTER.VERS:
Bel bows down, Nebo stoops; their idols are on the beasts, and on the cattle: the things that you

          {+}
         carried about are made a load, a burden to the weary [beast].

and even to old age, I am he, and even to hoar hairs I will carry [you

          {+}
        ]; I have made, and I will bear; yes, I will carry, and will deliver.

To whom will you

          {+}
         liken me, and make me equal, and compare me, that we may be like?

Remember this, and show yourselves men; bring it again to mind, O you

          {+}
         transgressors.

Listen to me, you

          {+}
         stout-hearted, who are far from righteousness:
